# =============================================================================
#  MQTT users
# =============================================================================
#  One line per person or system that connects to MQTT from OUTSIDE this stack:
#  a customer dashboard, Node-RED, a historian, a gateway with its own bridge.
#
#  ChirpStack's own internal connection is NOT listed here -- that one lives in
#  .env as MQTT_USERNAME / MQTT_PASSWORD. Leave it alone.
#
#  Format:     username    role
#  Roles:      integration      read application data only          <- most common
#              integration-rw   read application data, send downlinks
#              gateway          a gateway running its own bridge
#              gateway:EUI      the same, locked to one gateway ID
#
#  You never write MQTT permission rules yourself. The role does it.
#
#  TO ADD SOMEONE, either:
#      ./sitesync mqtt add acme-dashboard integration
#  or add the line here yourself and run ./sitesync apply -- either way the
#  password is generated and shown to you once.
#
#  Passwords are stored hashed and cannot be looked up later. That is on
#  purpose. If someone loses theirs, they do not need you:
#      ./sitesync mqtt reset acme-dashboard
# =============================================================================

# username              role
